  "transcriptText": "Welcome to The Player... the skills that protect everything else. Here's a question. You win more sessions than you lose. Can you still go broke? No... or yes?\n\nFirst, count your bankroll in buy-ins. Say you've got 2,000 chips. With a 100-chip buy-in, that's 20 buy-ins. At a 50-chip game, it's 40.\n\nNow, a toy model. Each session, you win or lose exactly one buy-in. This player wins 55% of them... an edge of a tenth of a buy-in a session. A winning player.\n\nSo how often does this player ever lose it all? From 5 buy-ins... 36.7%. From 10... 13.4%. From 20... 1.8%. From 40... 0.033%. Same player, same edge. Only the cushion changed.\n\nSo yes. A winning player can still go broke, with too few buy-ins. This is chips in a toy model, not money advice. Count in buy-ins... and keep enough that a bad run is a dip, not the end. Up next: tilt."
